v 3
d exactnl: Exact maximum likelihood estimation of the share-form nested logit
d
d Authors: Matthew J. Baker and Lisa M. George
d
d exactnl estimates the share-form nested logit demand model by exact
d maximum likelihood. The likelihood of the Berry (1994) log share-ratio
d includes a Jacobian term, (J-1)ln(1-sigma) per nest, that applied work
d omits. The omission has no effect when choice sets are fixed across
d markets but biases within-group substitution estimates when choice sets
d vary. exactnl includes the term, requires no instrument for the
d within-nest share, and supports fixed-effect absorption, a
d control-function price instrument, and a direct product-count
d (crowding) term in mean utility.
d
d If you use this command, please cite:
d Baker, Matthew J. and Lisa M. George. Demand Estimation with Variable
d Choice Sets: A Likelihood Correction for Nested Logit. Working paper.
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260710
d
f exactnl.ado
